---
// Privacy policy.
// A plain-language draft written from what this website actually does (contact form
// via Formspree, bookings via Calendly, no cookies or analytics). It has not been
// reviewed by a lawyer. If the site starts collecting anything else (analytics,
// newsletter sign-ups, new service providers), update this page at the same time.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const email = 'info@kavalirlabs.com';
const lastUpdated = '17 November 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | Kavalir Labs"
  description="How Kavalir Labs collects, uses and protects the personal information you share through kavalirlabs.com."
>
  <section aria-labelledby="privacy-heading" class="bg-navy-900 text-offwhite">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pb-16 pt-36 sm:pb-20">
      <h1
        id="privacy-heading"
        class="font-display text-4xl font-semibold leading-[1.1] tracking-tight sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl"
      >
        Privacy <span class="text-teal-400">Policy</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 text-base text-slate-blue-300">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="bg-offwhite text-navy-900">
    <div class="policy mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-20">
      <p>
        This policy explains what personal information Kavalir Labs collects through kavalirlabs.com,
        why we collect it and what your rights are. We collect as little as we can. This website has
        no user accounts, no advertising and no cookies.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Kavalir Labs is the trading name of a self-employed individual based in Malta. For the
        purposes of data protection law, Kavalir Labs is the controller of the personal information
        described in this policy. You can contact us about anything in this policy at <a
          href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect and why</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>When you send us a message through the contact form:</strong> your name, your email address
          and whatever you write in your message. We use this to reply to you and to discuss whether and
          how we can help.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>When you book a consultation:</strong> bookings are made on Calendly, a separate scheduling
          service. Calendly collects the details you enter there, such as your name, your email address
          and the time you choose, and passes them to us so that we can hold the call.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>When you email us:</strong> your email address and the contents of your email, so that
          we can reply.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>When you visit the website:</strong> like most websites, the company that hosts this site
          may automatically record technical information such as your IP address, your browser type and
          the pages requested, in order to deliver the site and keep it secure. We do not use this to identify
          you.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Please do not send us sensitive information, such as health details or passwords, through the
        contact form.
      </p>

      <h2>Our legal basis</h2>
      <p>We rely on the following legal bases under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR):</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          taking steps at your request before entering into a contract, when you ask about our services
          or book a consultation;
        </li>
        <li>
          our legitimate interests in responding to enquiries, running our business and keeping this website
          secure;
        </li>
        <li>legal obligation, where the law requires us to keep certain records.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
      <p>
        This website does not set cookies and does not use analytics, advertising or social media trackers.
        The contact form includes basic spam protection: with your message it sends the time the page
        was loaded and whether the browser appears to be automated. If you follow the link to Calendly,
        Calendly's own cookies and privacy policy apply on its site.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell your information or share it for marketing. We use a small number of service
        providers to run this website and handle enquiries:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Formspree</strong> (United States) receives contact form messages and delivers them to
          us by email.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Calendly</strong> (United States) handles consultation bookings.</li>
        <li>Our email and website hosting providers, which store our emails and deliver this website.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We may also disclose information where the law requires us to.</p>

      <h2>Transfers outside the European Economic Area</h2>
      <p>
        Formspree and Calendly are based in the United States, so information you submit through the
        contact form or a booking is transferred outside the European Economic Area. Where this happens,
        we rely on safeguards recognised by EU law, such as the EU-US Data Privacy Framework or standard
        contractual clauses.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        We keep your enquiry only for as long as we need it to deal with your request and any follow-up,
        and then delete it. If you become a client, or if the law requires us to keep records for longer
        (for example for tax purposes), we keep the relevant information for as long as that requires.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>ask for a copy of the information we hold about you;</li>
        <li>ask us to correct it;</li>
        <li>ask us to delete it;</li>
        <li>ask us to restrict how we use it, or object to our using it;</li>
        <li>receive it in a portable format.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To use any of these rights, email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. We will reply within
        one month.
      </p>
      <p>
        You also have the right to complain to a data protection regulator. In Malta this is the
        Information and Data Protection Commissioner (<a href="https://idpc.org.mt" rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >idpc.org.mt</a
        >). If you live elsewhere in the European Union, you can complain to the regulator in your own
        country.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        We take reasonable steps to protect your information, including using established service providers
        and limiting who can access it. No method of sending information over the internet is completely
        secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top of this page shows when it
        was last changed.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        If you have a question about this policy or about your information, email <a
          href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a
        >.
      </p>

      <p class="policy-back"><a href="/">Back to the home page</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* Text styles for the policy body. Colours come from the theme in global.css. */
  .policy {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--color-slate-blue-600);
  }

  .policy h2 {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    color: var(--color-navy-900);
  }

  .policy p,
  .policy ul {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .policy ul {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  .policy li + li {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .policy strong {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-navy-900);
  }

  .policy a {
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-teal-700);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }

  .policy a:hover {
    color: var(--color-navy-900);
  }

  .policy a:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-teal-700);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .policy .policy-back {
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }
</style>
